  python  grpc.Call.code, grpc.Call.details, grpc.RpcContext, grpc.RpcContext.add_callback, grpc.RpcContext.cancel, grpc.RpcContext.is_active, grpc.RpcContext.time_remaining, grpc.RpcError, grpc.RpcError.add_note, grpc.RpcError.args, grpc.RpcError.with_traceback, grpc.Status
  note    a call's failure is its status in a Reply, not a failure of the function, as Go's status.Error and Python's RpcError carry one; the rich details are bytes the program decodes with protobuf, where Go and Python need a generated google.rpc.Status

capability status/http-mapping  the status an HTTP status or an HTTP/2 reset stands for
  heroes  grpc.status_of_http, grpc.status_of_reset
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    gRPC's "HTTP to gRPC status code mapping": 400 INTERNAL, 401 UNAUTHENTICATED, 403 PERMISSION_DENIED, 404 UNIMPLEMENTED, 429/502/503/504 UNAVAILABLE; a CANCEL after the deadline is DEADLINE_EXCEEDED, as grpc-go's client reads it (observed against its server 2026-11-18)

capability status/message  grpc-message escaped and read back
  heroes  grpc.format_status_message, grpc.parse_status_message
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    "no such thing: ü 100%" read back whole by Go 1.27's grpc-go 1.85 and Python's grpcio 1.85, and theirs by this package (2026-11-18)

